        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9086585132> ;
    ns4:title "Relationship of Age and Exercise Performance in Patients With Heart Failure: the Hf-Action Study" ;
    ns6:abstract "More than three fourths of patients with heart failure (HF) are 65 years and older, and older age is associated with worse symptoms and prognoses than is younger age. Reduced exercise capacity is a chief HF complaint and indicates poorer prognosis, especially among elderly persons, but the mechanisms underlying functional decline in older patients with HF are largely unknown." ;
