<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n323634616> rdfs:label "Is early recurrence of hepatitis C associated with biliary anastomotic stricture after liver transplantation?" ;
    ns6:abstract "While the main effect of hepatitis C virus (HCV) is hepatitis, HCV is also known to cause a variety of systemic immunologic inflammatory abnormalities. The effect of HCV infection on the biliary tract after liver transplantation (LT) is not well understood. The aim of the current study is to determine if recurrence of hepatitis C affects biliary complications after LT, with special reference to late biliary anastomotic strictures (LBAS)." ;
