<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n367191884> rdfs:label "The Anti-Viral Effect of Sorafenib in Hepatitis C-Related Hepatocellular Carcinoma" ;
    ns6:abstract "Sorafenib is currently the only approved systemic therapy shown to have efficacy in the treatment of advanced hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC). Recent studies suggest that hepatitis C (HCV)-related HCC patients derive more clinical benefit from sorafenib than other subgroups, but the mechanism for this effect is unknown. In vitro data suggest that sorafenib may exert anti-viral properties, and thus our aim in this study was to evaluate potential anti-viral activity of sorafenib in patients with HCV-related HCC." ;
    ns6:pageStart "91" ;
    ns6:volume "37" ;
    ns3:grantCited "K24 CA139570",
