<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4013665057> rdfs:label "Is Postexcision, Preradiation Mammogram Necessary in Patients After Breast-Conserving Surgery With Negative Margins" ;
    ns6:abstract "In women with breast cancer and calcifications, controversy exists over the need for postexcision/lumpectomy, preradiation mammogram (PEM) after breast-conserving surgery (BCS). Further, the need for excision of remaining or suspicious calcifications after PEM when surgical margins are negative is unclear. We sought to characterize the utility of PEM hypothesizing that its value in directing the need for additional surgery is minimized after achieving negative surgical margins." ;
    ns6:pageStart "3205" ;
    ns6:volume "20" ;
