<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4469585955> rdfs:label "Phantom Shocks Unmasked: Clinical Data and Proposed Mechanism of Memory Reactivation of Past Traumatic Shocks in Patients With Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillators" ;
    ns4:creator <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1616932657>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n30859>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n3163097685>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n3621>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4820745184>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5392392606>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5931311221>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8372030780>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9887730694> ;
    ns4:title "Phantom Shocks Unmasked: Clinical Data and Proposed Mechanism of Memory Reactivation of Past Traumatic Shocks in Patients With Implantable Cardioverter Defibrillators" ;
    ns6:abstract "Implantable cardioverter defibrillators (ICD), despite an unequivocal clinical benefit, are known to have a complex psychosocial impact on the patients. ICD shocks and the resultant psychobiological changes are known to contribute to increased levels of anxiety, depression, and post-shock stress symptoms in these patients. Phantom shock is a patient-reported perception of an ICD shock in the absence of any actual shock; however, its pathophysiological understanding is poor." ;
    ns6:pageStart "205" ;
    ns6:volume "34" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.0" ;
    ns1:informationResourceInAuthorship <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n106242603>,
