<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n504339798> rdfs:label "Further psychometric properties of the Tourette's Disorder Scale-Parent Rated version (TODS-PR)." ;
    ns6:abstract "This study evaluated the psychometric properties of the Tourette's Disorder Scale-Parent Rated (TODS-PR), a 15-item parent-rated instrument that assesses a range of common symptoms seen in childhood Tourette's Disorder (TD) patients including tics, obsessions, compulsions, inattention, hyperactivity, aggression, and emotional disturbances. Participants were 67 children and adolescents ages 6-17 years who were diagnosed with TD and/or OCD and seen as a part of a larger study. Confirmatory factor analyses supported the original 4-factor structure of the TODS-PR with some slight re-specification of factor content. Internal consistencies were acceptable for the TODS-PR Total Score and factors. The TODS-PR Total Score and factors showed good convergent validity with other measures of symptomatology and impairment. These findings suggest that the TODS-PR is a reliable and valid parent-rating scale for assessing TD symptoms." ;
    ns6:number "2" ;
    ns6:volume "35" ;
    ns3:grantCited "K23MH01739",
        "R01 MH45802" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "PubMed-Harvester" ;
