        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n68245>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7015487860>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8687497069>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9804912569> ;
    ns4:title "Development of Autoantibodies in the Trialnet Natural History Study" ;
    ns6:abstract "Understanding the relationship between age and islet autoantibody (Ab) seroconversion can establish the optimal screening interval(s) to assess risk for type 1 diabetes, identify subjects who can participate in prevention trials, and determine associated costs. This study assessed the rates of seroconversion to glutamic acid decarboxylase positive (GAD65(+)), insulin positive (mIAA(+)), and insulinoma-associated protein 2 positive (ICA512(+)) in a large cohort of relatives of type 1 diabetes probands undergoing Ab rescreening in the TrialNet Natural History Study." ;
    ns6:pageStart "1897" ;
    ns6:volume "34" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.0" ;
    ns1:informationResourceInAuthorship <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1183955921>,
