<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6603912768> rdfs:label "Adaptive Expansion of the Maize Maternally Expressed Gene (Meg) Family Involves Changes in Expression Patterns and Protein Secondary Structures of Its Members" ;
    ns6:abstract "The Maternally expressed gene (Meg) family is a locally-duplicated gene family of maize which encodes cysteine-rich proteins (CRPs). The founding member of the family, Meg1, is required for normal development of the basal endosperm transfer cell layer (BETL) and is involved in the allocation of maternal nutrients to growing seeds. Despite the important roles of Meg1 in maize seed development, the evolutionary history of the Meg cluster and the activities of the duplicate genes are not understood." ;
    ns6:volume "14" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.3" ;
