        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9041172468>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n95594> ;
    ns4:title "Frequency of Kcnc3 Dna Variants as Causes of Spinocerebellar Ataxia 13 (Sca13)" ;
    ns6:abstract "Gain-of function or dominant-negative mutations in the voltage-gated potassium channel KCNC3 (Kv3.3) were recently identified as a cause of autosomal dominant spinocerebellar ataxia. Our objective was to describe the frequency of mutations associated with KCNC3 in a large cohort of index patients with sporadic or familial ataxia presenting to three US ataxia clinics at academic medical centers." ;
