<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n741364601> rdfs:label "Diffusion tensor imaging of frontal white matter and executive functioning in cocaine-exposed children." ;
    ns6:abstract "Although animal studies have demonstrated frontal white matter and behavioral changes resulting from prenatal cocaine exposure, no human studies have associated neuropsychological deficits in attention and inhibition with brain structure. We used diffusion tensor imaging to investigate frontal white matter integrity and executive functioning in cocaine-exposed children." ;
