        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6002815367>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7835915377>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7858322248> ;
    ns4:title "Brain Natriuretic Peptide Is Not Reno-Protective During Renal Ischemia-Reperfusion Injury in the Rat" ;
    ns6:abstract "Acute kidney injury (AKI) occurs in 30% of patients undergoing complex cardiovascular surgery, and renal ischemia-reperfusion (I/R) injury is often a contributing factor. A recent meta-analysis observed that perioperative natriuretic peptide administration was associated with a reduction in AKI requiring dialysis in cardiovascular surgery patients. This study was designed to further clarify the potential reno-protective effect of brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) using an established rat model of renal I/R injury." ;
    ns6:pageStart "E13" ;
    ns6:volume "164" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
