<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9773973114> rdfs:label "An Endogenous Bile Acid and Dietary Sucrose From Skin Secretions of Alkaloid-Sequestering Poison Frogs" ;
    ns4:creator <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1267337530>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n2432649837>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n34718>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n3520840639>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4298563214>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4611730137>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4738328327>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n64662>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n797263597> ;
    ns4:title "An Endogenous Bile Acid and Dietary Sucrose From Skin Secretions of Alkaloid-Sequestering Poison Frogs" ;
    ns6:abstract "The skins of Madagascar poison frogs (Mantella) and certain Neotropical poison frogs (Epipedobates, Dendrobates) secrete the new bile acid tauromantellic acid (1), which was found in both wild-caught and captive-born frogs. This is the first molecule of endogenous origin detected in skin secretions from these taxa. Sucrose was also detected in secretions from wild-caught Mantella but not in captive-born frogs, suggesting a dietary origin." ;
    ns6:pageStart "473" ;
    ns6:volume "75" ;
