        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8495854442>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8846593259>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9867237088> ;
    ns4:title "Diagnostic Accuracy of Quantitative Cardiac Mri Evaluation Compared To Stress Single-Photon-Emission Computed Tomography" ;
    ns6:abstract "Cardiac MRI (cMRI) perfusion is a promising non-invasive tool to assess myocardial ischemia. The accuracy of quantitative cMRI perfusion has been recently demonstrated, but to date no previous study has compared this technique with stress single-photon-emission computed tomography (SPECT). The aim of this study was to evaluate the diagnostic accuracy of myocardial perfusion reserve (MPR) based on cMRI compared with SPECT." ;
