        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7857390054>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9753474521> ;
    ns4:title "Messenger Rna Oxidation Occurs Early in Disease Pathogenesis and Promotes Motor Neuron Degeneration in Als" ;
    ns6:abstract "Accumulating evidence indicates that RNA oxidation is involved in a wide variety of neurological diseases and may be associated with neuronal deterioration during the process of neurodegeneration. However, previous studies were done in postmortem tissues or cultured neurons. Here, we used transgenic mice to demonstrate the role of RNA oxidation in the process of neurodegeneration." ;
    ns6:volume "3" ;
    ns3:grantCited "AG17317" ;
