        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8562594684>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9454999508> .

<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5087579368> rdfs:label "Role for Myosin-V Motor Proteins in the Selective Delivery of Kv Channel Isoforms To the Membrane Surface of Cardiac Myocytes" ;
    ns6:abstract "Kv1.5 (KCNA5) mediates the ultra-rapid delayed rectifier current that controls atrial action potential duration. Given its atrial-specific expression and alterations in human atrial fibrillation, Kv1.5 has emerged as a promising target for the treatment of atrial fibrillation. A necessary step in the development of novel agents that selectively modulate trafficking pathways is the identification of the cellular machinery controlling Kv1.5 surface density, of which little is yet known." ;
    ns6:number "6" ;
    ns6:pageStart "982" ;
    ns6:volume "114" ;
