        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8489552556>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n874990344> ;
    ns4:title "Worldwide Surgical Experience With the Paracor Heartnet Cardiac Restraint Device" ;
    ns6:abstract "An elastic ventricular restraint device has been developed for patients with heart failure who remain symptomatic despite treatment with standard therapies. The safety and efficacy of this device are under clinical investigation. Six-month data for the first 51 patients treated worldwide are reported. We hypothesize that the Paracor HeartNet device (Paracor Medical, Sunnyvale, Calif), placed through a minithoracotomy in patients with severe dilated cardiomyopathy, improves clinical and functional status." ;
