        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8255617798>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8817714296> ;
    ns4:title "Traceless Chemical Ligations From O-Acyl Serine Sites" ;
    ns6:abstract "Chemical ligation via O- to N-acyl transfer of O-acylated serine containing peptides affords serine containing native peptides via 8- and 11-membered cyclic transition states opening the door to a wide variety of potential applications to peptide elaboration. The feasibility of these traceless chemical ligations is feasible as supported by computation." ;
    ns6:pageStart "4836" ;
    ns6:volume "10" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.0" ;
