<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7858862053> rdfs:label "Levels of Alanine Aminotransferase Confound Use of Transient Elastography To Diagnose Fibrosis in Patients With Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection" ;
    ns6:abstract "Hepatic elastography (HE) is a noninvasive technique that measures liver stiffness and is used to diagnose hepatic fibrosis. It can help patients who are thought to have early-stage disease avoid a staging liver biopsy, but only when confounding variables that increase liver stiffness are excluded. Chronic inflammation from hepatitis C virus (HCV) infection is not considered to be one of these variables." ;
    ns6:pageStart "932" ;
    ns6:volume "10" ;
    ns3:grantCited "K24 CA139570-02",
