<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8142373900> rdfs:label "Resting State Changes in Functional Connectivity Correlate With Movement Recovery for Bci and Robot-Assisted Upper-Extremity Training After Stroke" ;
    ns6:abstract "Robot-assisted training may improve motor function in some hemiparetic patients after stroke, but no physiological predictor of rehabilitation progress is reliable. Resting state functional magnetic resonance imaging (RS-fMRI) may serve as a method to assess and predict changes in the motor network." ;
