    ns4:title "Brain Penetration Effects of Microelectrodes and Deep Brain Stimulation Leads in Ventral Intermediate Nucleus Stimulation for Essential Tremor" ;
    ns6:abstract "Microelectrode recording (MER) and macrostimulation (test stimulation) are used to refine the optimal deep brain stimulation (DBS) lead placement within the operative setting. It is well known that there can be a microlesion effect with microelectrode trajectories and DBS insertion. The aim of this study was to determine the impact of intraoperative MER and lead placement on tremor severity in a cohort of patients with essential tremor." ;
