<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n963927260> rdfs:label "Hyperthermia-Induced Disruption of Functional Connectivity in the Human Brain Network" ;
    ns6:abstract "Passive hyperthermia is a potential risk factor to human cognitive performance and work behavior in many extreme work environments. Previous studies have demonstrated significant effects of passive hyperthermia on human cognitive performance and work behavior. However, there is a lack of a clear understanding of the exact affected brain regions and inter-regional connectivities." ;
