    ns4:title "Vascular Smooth Muscle Jak2 Mediates Angiotensin Ii-Induced Hypertension Via Increased Levels of Reactive Oxygen Species" ;
    ns6:abstract "Angiotensin II (Ang II) type AT(1) receptors expressed on vascular smooth muscle cells (VSMCs) couple to the Jak2 signalling pathway. However, the importance of this tissue-specific coupling is poorly understood. The purpose of this investigation was to determine the importance of VSMC-derived Jak2 in angiotensin II-mediated hypertension." ;
