<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1278917051> rdfs:label "Toll-Like Receptor 3 Ligand, Polyic, Induces Proteinuria and Glomerular Cd80, and Increases Urinary Cd80 in Mice" ;
    ns6:abstract "We have reported that children with biopsy-proven minimal change disease (MCD) express CD80 (also known as B7.1) in their podocytes and excrete high levels of CD80 in their urine during active nephrotic syndrome. We also reported that polyIC, a Toll-like receptor 3 ligand, increases CD80 mRNA and protein expression in cultured human podocytes dose-dependently, with actin re-organization and a reduction in synaptopodin expression." ;
    ns6:pageStart "1439" ;
    ns6:volume "28" ;
