<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4261524366> rdfs:label "Prognostic Significance of Interleukin-6 Single Nucleotide Polymorphism Genotypes in Neuroblastoma: Rs1800795 (Promoter) and Rs8192284 (Receptor)" ;
    ns6:abstract "Neuroblastoma is a childhood cancer of the sympathetic nervous system and many patients present with high-risk disease. Risk stratification, based on pathology and tumor-derived biomarkers, has improved prediction of clinical outcomes, but overall survival (OS) rates remain unfavorable and new therapeutic targets are needed. Some studies suggest a link between interleukin (IL)-6 and more aggressive behavior in neuroblastoma tumor cells. Therefore, we examined the impact of two IL-6 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNP) on neuroblastoma disease progression." ;
    ns6:pageStart "5234" ;
    ns6:volume "15" ;
    ns3:grantCited "L40 CA124221-02" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
