<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7203942163> rdfs:label "Detection of Colonic Dysplasia in Vivo Using a Targeted Heptapeptide and Confocal Microendoscopy" ;
    ns4:creator <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1043570>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n2401783148>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4458332187>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7014675826>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7312495539>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7400534707>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7688893941>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n929831306>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9520373448>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n989804958>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9973995449> ;
    ns4:title "Detection of Colonic Dysplasia in Vivo Using a Targeted Heptapeptide and Confocal Microendoscopy" ;
    ns6:abstract "A combination of targeted probes and new imaging technologies provides a powerful set of tools with the potential to improve the early detection of cancer. To develop a probe for detecting colon cancer, we screened phage display peptide libraries against fresh human colonic adenomas for high-affinity ligands with preferential binding to premalignant tissue. We identified a specific heptapeptide sequence, VRPMPLQ, which we synthesized, conjugated with fluorescein and tested in patients undergoing colonoscopy. We imaged topically administered peptide using a fluorescence confocal microendoscope delivered through the instrument channel of a standard colonoscope. In vivo images were acquired at 12 frames per second with 50-microm working distance and 2.5-microm (transverse) and 20-microm (axial) resolution. The fluorescein-conjugated peptide bound more strongly to dysplastic colonocytes than to adjacent normal cells with 81% sensitivity and 82% specificity. This methodology represents a promising diagnostic imaging approach for the early detection of colorectal cancer and potentially of other epithelial malignancies." ;
    ns6:pageStart "454" ;
    ns6:volume "14" ;
    ns3:grantCited "K08 DK067618",
        "K08 DK067618-06",
        "P30 DK56339",
        "R03 DK075603",
        "R03 DK075603-03",
        "U54 CA105296",
        "U54 CA136429",
        "U54 CA136429-01" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.0" ;
