<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7830952120> rdfs:label "The Significance of a Marginal Excision After Preoperative Radiation Therapy for Soft Tissue Sarcoma of the Extremity" ;
    ns6:abstract "Marginal excision of soft tissue sarcoma (STS), defined as resection through the tumor pseudocapsule or surrounding reactive tissue, increases the likelihood of local recurrence and necessitates re-excision or postoperative radiation. However, its impact after preoperative radiation therapy (RT) remains unclear. This study therefore investigated the significance of marginal margins in patients treated with preoperative RT for extremity STS, reporting long-term local control and limb preservation endpoints." ;
    ns6:pageStart "3199" ;
    ns6:volume "118" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.0" ;
