<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9195096580> rdfs:label "Ultrasound and Magnetic Resonance Imaging in the Evaluation of Psoriatic Dactylitis: Status and Perspectives" ;
    ns6:abstract "Dactylitis, a characteristic feature of the spondyloarthropathies, occurs in up to 48% of patients with psoriatic arthritis (PsA). No clear consensus on the underlying components and pathogenesis of dactylitis exists in the literature. We undertook a systematic review of ultrasound (US) and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) literature to better define imaging elements that contribute to the dactylitic digit seen in PsA. Our objectives were to determine first the level of homogeneity of each imaging modality's definition of the components of dactylitis, and second, to evaluate the metric properties of each imaging modality according to the Outcome Measures in Rheumatology Clinical Trials (OMERACT) filter." ;
    ns6:number "12" ;
    ns6:pageStart "1951" ;
    ns6:volume "40" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.3" ;
    ns1:informationResourceInAuthorship <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1276260831>,
