        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n510903744>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5252138076>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n528937920>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8368617850> ;
    ns4:title "Persistent Orofacial Muscle Pain" ;
    ns6:abstract "The pathophysiology of persistent orofacial myalgia has been the centre of much controversy. In this article we suggest a novel descriptive term; 'persistent orofacial muscle pain' (POMP) and review current evidence that supports the hypothesis that the induction of POMP involves the interplay between a peripheral nociceptive source in muscle, a faulty central nervous system component and decreased coping ability. In this context it is widely accepted that a complex interaction of variable intrinsic and extrinsic factors act to induce POMP and dysfunction." ;
    ns6:pageStart "23" ;
    ns6:volume "17" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
