<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1561718717> rdfs:label "TGF-beta induces proangiogenic and antiangiogenic factors via parallel but distinct Smad pathways." ;
    ns6:abstract "Angiogenesis has a key role in numerous disease processes. One of the most important angiogenic factors is vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF-A), whereas thrombospondin-1 (TSP-1) is a major antiangiogenic factor. Recent studies have shown that VEGF-A as well as TSP-1 is regulated by transforming growth factor-beta1 (TGF-beta1), but the mechanism remains unclear." ;
    ns6:number "2" ;
    ns6:volume "66" ;
    ns3:grantCited "DK-52121" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "PubMed-Harvester" ;
