<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n2425194908> rdfs:label "Serum From Minimal Change Patients in Relapse Increases Cd80 Expression in Cultured Podocytes" ;
    ns6:abstract "Minimal change disease (MCD) is the most common cause of nephrotic syndrome in children and is associated with the expression of CD80 in podocytes and the increased excretion of CD80 in urine. We hypothesized that serum from patients with MCD might stimulate CD80 expression in cultured podocytes." ;
