        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6477535856>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6910136164>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7220009131> ;
    ns4:title "Imaging Short- and Long-Term Training Success in Chronic Aphasia" ;
    ns6:abstract "To date, functional imaging studies of treatment-induced recovery from chronic aphasia only assessed short-term treatment effects after intensive language training. In the present study, we show with functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI), that different brain regions may be involved in immediate versus long-term success of intensive language training in chronic post-stroke aphasia patients." ;
    ns6:volume "10" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
