<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4057554027> rdfs:label "Identification of a Novel Inhibitor of Jak2 Tyrosine Kinase By Structure-Based Virtual Screening" ;
    ns6:abstract "Janus kinase 2 (JAK2) plays a crucial role in the pathomechanism of myeloproliferative disorders and hematologic malignancies. A somatic mutation of JAK2 (Val617Phe) was previously shown to occur in 98% of patients with polycythemia vera and 50% of patients with essential thrombocythemia and primary myelofibrosis. Thus, effective JAK2 kinase inhibitors may be of significant therapeutic importance. Here, we applied a structure-based virtual screen to identify novel JAK2 inhibitors. One JAK2 inhibitor in particular, G6, demonstrated remarkable potency as well as specificity, which makes it as a potential lead candidate against diseases related to elevated JAK2 tyrosine kinase activity." ;
    ns6:pageStart "3598" ;
    ns6:volume "19" ;
