        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7816583446>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8832122230> ;
    ns4:title "European Ancestry and Resting Metabolic Rate in Older African Americans" ;
    ns6:abstract "Resting metabolic rate (RMR) contributes 60-80% of total energy expenditure and is consistently lower in populations of African descent compared with populations of European populations. Determination of European ancestry (EA) through single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) analysis would provide an initial step for identifying genetic associations that contribute to low RMR. We sought to evaluate the association between RMR and EA in African Americans." ;
    ns6:pageStart "663" ;
    ns6:volume "65" ;
    ns3:grantCited "N01-AG-6-2101",
