<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5343121685> rdfs:label "Carla Task Force On Sarcopenia: Propositions for Clinical Trials" ;
    ns6:abstract "Digoxin is frequently used for rate control of atrial fibrillation (AF). It has, however, been associated with increased mortality. It remains unclear whether digoxin itself is responsible for the increased mortality (toxic drug effect) or whether it is prescribed to sicker patients with inherently higher mortality due to comorbidities. The goal of our study was to determine the relationship between digoxin and mortality in patients with AF." ;
    ns6:pageStart "700" ;
    ns6:volume "13" ;
