        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n2663703248>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4202961747>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5048453970>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5183467216>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5272747388>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7039788258>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7087196052> ;
    ns4:title "Prognostic Value of Virological and Immunological Responses After 6 Months of Antiretroviral Treatment in Adults With Hiv-1 Infection in Sub-Saharan Africa" ;
    ns6:abstract "HIV RNA monitoring is not available in most antiretroviral treatment (ART) programs in sub-Saharan Africa; switch to second-line therapy is mostly guided by clinical/immunological criteria. This may lead to unnecessary disease progression and drug resistance accumulation. We investigated the prognostic value of virological and immunological status 6 months after ART initiation with respect to death, loss to follow-up, and treatment switch." ;
    ns6:pageStart "236" ;
    ns6:volume "59" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.0" ;
