    ns4:title "Large Candidate Gene Association Study Reveals Genetic Risk Factors and Therapeutic Targets for Fibromyalgia" ;
    ns6:abstract "Fibromyalgia (FM) represents a complex disorder that is characterized by widespread pain and tenderness and is frequently accompanied by additional somatic and cognitive/affective symptoms. Genetic risk factors are known to contribute to the etiology of the syndrome. The aim of this study was to examine >350 genes for association with FM, using a large-scale candidate gene approach." ;
