<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6784410317> rdfs:label "Intra-Articular Gene Delivery and Expression of Interleukin-1Ra Mediated By Self-Complementary Adeno-Associated Virus" ;
    ns6:abstract "The adeno-associated virus (AAV) has many safety features that favor its use in the treatment of arthritic conditions; however, the conventional, single-stranded vector is inefficient for gene delivery to fibroblastic cells that primarily populate articular tissues. This has been attributed to the inability of these cells to convert the vector to a double-stranded form. To overcome this, we evaluated double-stranded self-complementary (sc) AAV as a vehicle for intra-articular gene delivery." ;
    ns6:pageStart "605" ;
    ns6:volume "11" ;
    ns3:grantCited "AR048566",
