        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n88556> ;
    ns4:title "Inspiratory Muscle Strength Training Improves Weaning Outcome in Failure To Wean Patients: a Randomized Trial" ;
    ns6:abstract "Most patients are readily liberated from mechanical ventilation (MV) support, however, 10% - 15% of patients experience failure to wean (FTW). FTW patients account for approximately 40% of all MV days and have significantly worse clinical outcomes. MV induced inspiratory muscle weakness has been implicated as a contributor to FTW and recent work has documented inspiratory muscle weakness in humans supported with MV." ;
    ns6:volume "15" ;
