<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7945948021> rdfs:label "Addition of Exogenous Nad(+) Prevents Mefloquine-Induced Neuroaxonal and Hair Cell Degeneration Through Reduction of Caspase-3-Mediated Apoptosis in Cochlear Organotypic Cultures" ;
    ns6:abstract "Mefloquine is widely used for the treatment of malaria. However, this drug is known to induce neurological side effects including depression, anxiety, balance disorder, and sensorineural hearing loss. Yet, there is currently no treatment for these side effects." ;
