    ns4:title "Comorbid Depression and Anxiety Symptoms as Predictors of Cardiovascular Events: Results From the Nhlbi-Sponsored Women's Ischemia Syndrome Evaluation (Wise) Study" ;
    ns6:abstract "To study the independent and interactive effects of depression and anxiety symptoms as predictors of cardiovascular disease (CVD) events in a sample of women with suspected myocardial ischemia. Symptoms of depression and anxiety overlap strongly and are independent predictors of CVD events. Although these symptoms commonly co-occur in medical patients, little is known about combined effects of depression and anxiety on CVD risk." ;
