    ns4:title "Toll-Like Receptor 3 Ligands Induce Cd80 Expression in Human Podocytes Via An Nf-Kappa B-Dependent Pathway" ;
    ns6:abstract "Recent studies suggest that CD80 (also known as B7.1) is expressed on podocytes in minimal-change disease (MCD) and may have a role in mediating proteinuria. CD80 expression is known to be induced by Toll-like receptor (TLR) ligands in dendritic cells. We therefore evaluated the ability of TLR to induce CD80 in human cultured podocytes." ;
