    ns4:title "Dhea-S Levels and Cardiovascular Disease Mortality in Postmenopausal Women: Results From the National Institutes of Health-National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (Nhlbi)-Sponsored Women's Ischemia Syndrome Evaluation (Wise)" ;
    ns6:abstract "Dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate (DHEA-S), a major circulating sex steroid prohormone, declines with age. Low levels have been associated with increased cardiovascular disease (CVD) risk and all-cause mortality, although these results have not been consistently replicated, particularly in women." ;
