        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7532434635>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8507297459>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9048641163>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9117854677> ;
    ns4:title "Chd5, a Tumor Suppressor Gene Deleted From 1P36.31 in Neuroblastomas" ;
    ns6:abstract "Neuroblastomas are characterized by hemizygous 1p deletions, suggesting that a tumor suppressor gene resides in this region. We previously mapped the smallest region of consistent deletion to a 2-Mb region of 1p36.31 that encodes 23 genes. Based on mutation analysis, expression pattern, and putative function, we identified CHD5 as the best tumor suppressor gene candidate." ;
    ns6:pageStart "940" ;
    ns6:volume "100" ;
