    ns4:title "Notch1 and Notch3 Coordinate Esophageal Squamous Differentiation Through a Csl-Dependent Transcriptional Network" ;
    ns6:abstract "The Notch receptor family regulates cell fate through cell-cell communication. CSL (CBF-1/RBP-jκ, Su(H), Lag-1) drives canonical Notch-mediated gene transcription during cell lineage specification, differentiation, and proliferation in the hematopoietic system, the intestine, the pancreas, and the skin. However, the functional roles of Notch in esophageal squamous epithelial biology are unknown." ;
