<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6374672045> rdfs:label "The Society of Thoracic Surgeons 2008 Cardiac Surgery Risk Models: Part 3-Valve Plus Coronary Artery Bypass Grafting Surgery" ;
    ns6:abstract "Since 1999, The Society of Thoracic Surgeons (STS) has published two risk models that can be used to adjust the results of valve surgery combined with coronary artery bypass graft surgery (CABG). The most recent was developed from data for patients who had surgery between 1994 and 1997 using operative mortality as the only endpoint. Furthermore, this model did not specifically consider mitral valve repair plus CABG, an increasingly common procedure. Consistent with STS policy of periodically updating and improving its risk models, new models for valve surgery combined with CABG have been developed. These models specifically address both perioperative morbidity and mitral valve repair, and they are based on contemporary data." ;
    ns6:pageStart "S43" ;
    ns6:volume "88" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
    ns1:informationResourceInAuthorship <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1261600822>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1467302081>,
