        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n34003>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6754866755>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7344026683>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n793354139>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8385>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n883938760>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9583642862>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9656775876> ;
    ns4:title "A Randomized Controlled Trial of Low-Dose Hormone Therapy On Myocardial Ischemia in Postmenopausal Women With No Obstructive Coronary Artery Disease: Results From the National Institutes of Health/National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute-Sponsored Women's Ischemia Syndrome Evaluation (Wise)" ;
    ns6:abstract "Compared with men, women have more evidence of myocardial ischemia with no obstructive coronary artery disease. Although low endogenous estrogen levels are associated with endothelial dysfunction, the role of low-dose hormone therapy has not been fully evaluated. We postulate that a 12-week duration of low-dose hormone replacement therapy is associated with myocardial ischemia and endothelial dysfunction." ;
