        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9304610637> ;
    ns4:title "Alpha(1)-Antitrypsin Deficiency-Related Alleles Z and S and the Risk of Wegener's Granulomatosis" ;
    ns6:abstract "Deficiency of α(1) -antitrypsin (α(1) AT) may be a determinant of susceptibility to Wegener's granulomatosis (WG). Several previous, mainly small, case-control studies have shown that 5-27% of patients with WG carried the α(1) AT deficiency Z allele. It is not clear whether the S allele, the other major α(1) AT deficiency variant, is associated with WG. This study investigated the relationship of the α(1) AT deficiency Z and S alleles with the risk of developing WG in a large cohort." ;
    ns6:pageStart "3760" ;
    ns6:volume "62" ;
