<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7445659811> rdfs:label "Hypertension Susceptibility Loci and Blood Pressure Response To Antihypertensives Results From the Pharmacogenomic Evaluation of Antihypertensive Responses Study" ;
    ns6:abstract "To date, 39 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) have been associated with blood pressure (BP) or hypertension in genome-wide association studies in whites. Our hypothesis is that the loci/SNPs associated with BP/hypertension are also associated with BP response to antihypertensive drugs." ;
