<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8302814609> rdfs:label "Coronary Bypass Surgery With Or Without Surgical Ventricular Reconstruction" ;
    ns6:abstract "Surgical ventricular reconstruction is a specific procedure designed to reduce left ventricular volume in patients with heart failure caused by coronary artery disease. We conducted a trial to address the question of whether surgical ventricular reconstruction added to coronary-artery bypass grafting (CABG) would decrease the rate of death or hospitalization for cardiac causes, as compared with CABG alone." ;
