<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9274047759> rdfs:label "Mr-Impact Ii: Magnetic Resonance Imaging for Myocardial Perfusion Assessment in Coronary Artery Disease Trial: Perfusion-Cardiac Magnetic Resonance Vs. Single-Photon Emission Computed Tomography for the Detection of Coronary Artery Disease: a Comparative Multicentre, Multivendor Trial" ;
    ns6:abstract "Perfusion-cardiac magnetic resonance (CMR) has emerged as a potential alternative to single-photon emission computed tomography (SPECT) to assess myocardial ischaemia non-invasively. The goal was to compare the diagnostic performance of perfusion-CMR and SPECT for the detection of coronary artery disease (CAD) using conventional X-ray coronary angiography (CXA) as the reference standard." ;
