    ns1:mailingAddress <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n85428> ;
    ns1:preferredTitle "Associate Professor" ;
    ns1:teachingOverview "I teach yearly in the three semester Pharmacology series for first and second year Pharmacy students and coordinate the first course in this series.&nbsp; I also give yearly lectures in Physiological Basis of Disease for first year pharmacy students.&nbsp; My student evaluations are above average and I was elected for &ldquo;Teacher of the Year&rdquo; for 2007.&nbsp; I lecture yearly in an undergraduate Honors course in Pharmacy and have directed research projects for numerous undergraduate Pharmacy students, undergraduate IDS majors, senior clerkship students and a Fullbright Scholar from the University of Frankfurt resulting in a number of publications. In terms of graduate educa&not;tion,&nbsp; I&nbsp; coordinate and teach&nbsp;&nbsp; &ldquo;Neurochemical Foundation of Phar&not;macodynamics&rdquo;,&nbsp; I&nbsp; lecture&nbsp; in&nbsp;&nbsp; &ldquo;Research Techniques in Pharmacodynamics&rdquo;, and I developed, coordinate and teach &ldquo;The Pharmacodynamics of Drugs of Abuse&rdquo;.&nbsp; I have supervised five&nbsp; Ph.D. students through matriculation,&nbsp; fourteen doctoral students in their research rotations and&nbsp; three post-doctoral fellows.&nbsp;" ;
    ns5:lastName "Peris" .

