        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n6792853138>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8118333739>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8385>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n883938760>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9352015692> ;
    ns4:title "Relationships Between Cardiovascular Disease Risk Factors and Depressive Symptoms as Predictors of Cardiovascular Disease Events in Women" ;
    ns6:abstract "Modifiable risk factors for cardiovascular disease (CVD) account for much of the variability in CVD outcomes and are also related to psychosocial variables. There is evidence that depression can undermine the treatment and advance the progression of CVD risk factors, suggesting that CVD risk factor relationships with CVD events may differ among those with depression." ;
    ns6:pageStart "133" ;
    ns6:volume "21" ;
