    ns4:title "A Prognostic Model for Estimating the Time To Virologic Failure in Hiv-1 Infected Patients Undergoing a New Combination Antiretroviral Therapy Regimen" ;
    ns6:abstract "HIV-1 genotypic susceptibility scores (GSSs) were proven to be significant prognostic factors of fixed time-point virologic outcomes after combination antiretroviral therapy (cART) switch/initiation. However, their relative-hazard for the time to virologic failure has not been thoroughly investigated, and an expert system that is able to predict how long a new cART regimen will remain effective has never been designed." ;
