    ns4:title "Overcoming Qeeg Abnormalities and Reward Gene Deficits During Protracted Abstinence in Male Psychostimulant and Polydrug Abusers Utilizing Putative Dopamine D(2) Agonist Therapy: Part 2" ;
    ns6:abstract "It is well established that in both food- and drug-addicted individuals there is \"dopamine resistance\" associated with the DRD2 gene A1 allele. Based on earlier studies, evidence is emerging wherein the potential of utilizing a natural, nonaddicting, safe, putative D2 agonist may play a significant role in the recovery of individuals with reward deficiency syndrome, including those addicted to psychoactive chemicals." ;
