        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8616753875>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8732825591>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9001432910> ;
    ns4:title "Genetic Variation At Cr1 Increases Risk of Cerebral Amyloid Angiopathy" ;
    ns6:abstract "Accumulated evidence suggests that a variant within the CR1 gene (single nucleotide polymorphism rs6656401), known to increase risk for Alzheimer disease (AD), influences β-amyloid (Aβ) deposition in brain tissue. Given the biologic overlap between AD and cerebral amyloid angiopathy (CAA), a leading cause of intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH) in elderly individuals, we investigated whether rs6656401 increases the risk of CAA-related ICH and influences vascular Aβ deposition." ;
    ns6:pageStart "334" ;
    ns6:volume "78" ;
