        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7124143064>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n7388585366>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n777097408>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8599326>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9321159> ;
    ns4:title "Ubiquitin C-Terminal Hydrolase Is a Novel Biomarker in Humans for Severe Traumatic Brain Injury" ;
    ns6:abstract "Ubiquitin C-terminal hydrolase (UCH-L1), also called neuronal-specific protein gene product (PGP 9.3), is highly abundant in neurons. To assess the reliability of UCH-L1 as a potential biomarker for traumatic brain injury (TBI) this study compared cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) levels of UCH-L1 from adult patients with severe TBI to uninjured controls; and examined the relationship between levels with severity of injury, complications and functional outcome." ;
    ns6:pageStart "138" ;
    ns6:volume "38" ;
    ns3:grantCited "R01 NS052831" ;
