<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n3455713201> rdfs:label "Is Diabetes Mellitus-Linked Amino Acid Signature Associated With Beta-Blocker-Induced Impaired Fasting Glucose?" ;
    ns6:abstract "The 5-amino acid (AA) signature, including isoleucine, leucine, valine, tyrosine, and phenylalanine, has been associated with incident diabetes mellitus and insulin resistance. We investigated whether this same AA signature, single-nucleotide polymorphisms in genes in their catabolic pathway, was associated with development of impaired fasting glucose (IFG) after atenolol treatment." ;
