<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8396775951> rdfs:label "Declining Prevalence of Hiv-1 Drug Resistance in Antiretroviral Treatment-Exposed Individuals in Western Europe" ;
    ns6:abstract "HIV-1 drug resistance represents a major obstacle to infection and disease control. This retrospective study analyzes trends and determinants of resistance in antiretroviral treatment (ART)-exposed individuals across 7 countries in Europe. Of 20 323 cases, 80% carried at least one resistance mutation: these declined from 81% in 1997 to 71% in 2008. Predicted extensive 3-class resistance was rare (3.2% considering the cumulative genotype) and peaked at 4.5% in 2005, decreasing thereafter. The proportion of cases exhausting available drug options dropped from 32% in 2000 to 1% in 2008. Reduced risk of resistance over calendar years was confirmed by multivariable analysis." ;
    ns6:pageStart "1216" ;
    ns6:volume "207" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
