<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n89735> rdfs:label "In vivo silencing of alpha-synuclein using naked siRNA"^^xsd:string ;
    ns6:abstract "Overexpression of alpha-synuclein (SNCA) in families with multiplication mutations causes parkinsonism and subsequent dementia, characterized by diffuse Lewy Body disease post-mortem. Genetic variability in SNCA contributes to risk of idiopathic Parkinson's disease (PD), possibly as a result of overexpression. SNCA downregulation is therefore a valid therapeutic target for PD." ;
