<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n5672063370> rdfs:label "Mass Media Health Communication Campaigns Combined With Health-Related Product Distribution a Community Guide Systematic Review" ;
    ns6:abstract "Health communication campaigns including mass media and health-related product distribution have been used to reduce mortality and morbidity through behavior change. The intervention is defined as having two core components reflecting two social marketing principles: (1) promoting behavior change through multiple communication channels, one being mass media, and (2) distributing a free or reduced-price product that facilitates adoption and maintenance of healthy behavior change, sustains cessation of harmful behaviors, or protects against behavior-related disease or injury." ;
    ns6:number "3" ;
    ns6:pageStart "360" ;
    ns6:volume "47" ;
