    ns4:title "Efficacy and Safety of Sirolimus in Lymphangioleiomyomatosis" ;
    ns6:abstract "Lymphangioleiomyomatosis (LAM) is a progressive, cystic lung disease in women; it is associated with inappropriate activation of mammalian target of rapamycin (mTOR) signaling, which regulates cellular growth and lymphangiogenesis. Sirolimus (also called rapamycin) inhibits mTOR and has shown promise in phase 1-2 trials involving patients with LAM." ;
    ns6:pageStart "1595" ;
    ns6:volume "364" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
