<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n3550067319> rdfs:label "Hyperphagia: Current Concepts and Future Directions Proceedings of the 2Nd International Conference On Hyperphagia" ;
    ns6:abstract "Hyperphagia is a central feature of inherited disorders (e.g., Prader-Willi Syndrome) in which obesity is a primary phenotypic component. Hyperphagia may also contribute to obesity as observed in the general population, thus raising the potential importance of common underlying mechanisms and treatments. Substantial gaps in understanding the molecular basis of inherited hyperphagia syndromes are present as are a lack of mechanistic of mechanistic targets that can serve as a basis for pharmacologic and behavioral treatments." ;
    ns6:number "1" ;
    ns6:pageStart "S1" ;
    ns6:volume "22" ;
    ns3:grantCited "K01 DA031230" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.3" ;
