<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8889258145> rdfs:label "Polyanalgesic Consensus Conference-2012: Recommendations To Reduce Morbidity and Mortality in Intrathecal Drug Delivery in the Treatment of Chronic Pain" ;
    ns6:abstract "Targeted intrathecal drug infusion to treat moderate to severe chronic pain has become a standard part of treatment algorithms when more conservative options fail. This therapy is well established in the literature, has shown efficacy, and is an important tool for the treatment of both cancer and noncancer pain; however, it has become clear in recent years that intrathecal drug delivery is associated with risks for serious morbidity and mortality." ;
    ns6:pageStart "467" ;
    ns6:volume "15" ;
    ns3:harvestedBy "Python Pubs version 1.1" ;
    ns1:informationResourceInAuthorship <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n134643182>,
