        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9994975149> ;
    ns4:title "A Physical Map for the Amborella Trichopoda Genome Sheds Light On the Evolution of Angiosperm Genome Structure" ;
    ns6:abstract "Recent phylogenetic analyses have identified Amborella trichopoda, an understory tree species endemic to the forests of New Caledonia, as sister to a clade including all other known flowering plant species. The Amborella genome is a unique reference for understanding the evolution of angiosperm genomes because it can serve as an outgroup to root comparative analyses. A physical map, BAC end sequences and sample shotgun sequences provide a first view of the 870 Mbp Amborella genome." ;
    ns6:volume "12" ;
