    ns4:title "Effect of Intracoronary Delivery of Autologous Bone Marrow Mononuclear Cells 2 To 3 Weeks Following Acute Myocardial Infarction On Left Ventricular Function the Latetime Randomized Trial" ;
    ns6:abstract "Clinical trial results suggest that intracoronary delivery of autologous bone marrow mononuclear cells (BMCs) may improve left ventricular (LV) function when administered within the first week following myocardial infarction (MI). However, because a substantial number of patients may not present for early cell delivery, the efficacy of autologous BMC delivery 2 to 3 weeks post-MI warrants investigation." ;
    ns6:pageStart "2110" ;
    ns6:volume "306" ;
